{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Classification keys: grouping living things","theme":{"background":"#f4f9f1","foreground":"#1d3b22","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Classification key"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"A set of yes or no questions that helps you identify and name a living thing by following its features."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"leaf"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Living things"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Things that grow, need food, breathe and reproduce. Plants and animals are both living things."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which group does a fish belong to?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Birds","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Fish","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Insects","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"cat"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Which feature do mammals have that most other animals do not?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Scales","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Fur or hair","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Feathers","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-d","label":"Shells","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Your class finds a small creature under a stone in the school garden. It has six legs. Which way will you use the key?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Check if it has a backbone","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Check if it has six legs first","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"No backbone, so the key leads you to the invertebrates. You find it is a beetle, an insect. Well done."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Six legs means an insect. The key narrows it down to a beetle. Good thinking."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"What is the first thing to do when you use a classification key?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Guess the name","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Read the first pair of questions","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Pick the biggest picture","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"fish"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Does a fish breathe with lungs or gills?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Lungs","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Gills","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which of these is a plant?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Oak tree","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Mushroom","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Earthworm","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done, you finished the classification keys stack!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Keys help us group and name living things. Keep using them outside and in class."}],"actions":[]}}
